Description: pvr: raise maxTexelBufferElements to what the descriptor holds
 A texel buffer view is a linear 2D texture PVR_BUFFER_VIEW_WIDTH (8192)
 texels wide with one row per 8192 elements (pvr_CreateBufferView()); pco
 turns the element index into (index % 8192, index / 8192) for both the
 sampled and the storage path. The row count is bounded by the 2D texture
 height, so report PVR_BUFFER_VIEW_WIDTH * max_render_size instead of
 64 Ki. With 64 Ki, st/mesa on zink rejects its GPU path for PBO uploads
 larger than that (st_pbo_addresses_setup() against MaxTextureBufferSize)
 and copies through a CPU mapping of the buffer instead.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
